**EXERCISE 5.7.** Find definitions of

$$\lambda x, y.\, \tau \quad \text{and} \quad \sigma(x, y)$$

which use only $\lambda v$ with one variable and applications only to one argument at a time. Note that use must be made of the combinators $p_0$, $p_1$, pair. Generalize the result to functions of many variables.

The development is with the
[multi-argument λ-abstraction](1980_multiLam.md) peer.

<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`example_507`).** Binary λ-abstraction and application are curry and successive evaluation; uncurry inverts curry; pairing is recovered from its projections; ternary curry evaluates by nested pairs.

*Proof.* Assemble `lam_two_vars`, `app_two_args`, `uncurry_lam_two_vars`, `surjective_pairing`, and `curry₃_apply` from the multi-argument λ peer. ∎
